1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
Exam day - what do you do?
考试日——你会做些什么呢？

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,290
I take a ring my grandfather gave me to the exam.
我会带着爷爷给我的一枚戒指去参加考试。

3
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:11,720
It's a reminder of his affection and gives me a sense of security and calms my nerves.
它是爷爷关爱的一种提醒，能给我一种安全感，让我放松下来。

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:16,010
My brother makes a fuss about wearing his green underwear.
我的哥哥会小题大做穿上他的绿色内裤。

5
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:19,450
He's not alone in placing his hopes in a garment.
并非只有他一个人把希望寄托在一件衣物上。

6
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:29,210
One in three students admitted to wearing 'good luck underwear' to try to boost exam chances, according to a poll for pen makers, Bic.
根据钢笔制造商比克（Bic）开展的一项民意调查，三分之一的学生承认会穿“幸运内裤”，试图提高考试通过的几率。

7
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:42,900
The same poll suggested that 60% of students change their diet before a test in the hope that it can increase their brain power and memory – oily fish and fruit and vegetables are at the top of the list.
同一项民意调查显示，60%的学生在考试前会改变饮食，希望能提高他们的脑力和记忆力——富含脂肪的鱼以及水果和蔬菜在他们的饮食清单中位居前列。

8
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:50,720
This is good as long as you don't stuff your face with junk food all year long and decide to go healthy just for the exam.
只要你不是一整年都狂吃垃圾食品，只是为了考试才决定吃得健康些，这样做还是不错的。

9
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:57,840
Making the extra effort to succeed is good but if you haven't put in the hours of study, nothing will help you.
为取得成功付出额外努力是好的，但如果你没有投入学习时间，什么都帮不了你。

10
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:15,020
Patrick Wilson, former teacher and founder of a private tuition firm, says: "The best way to feel truly confident and help beat that stomach-churning exam angst is to prepare for each exam in advance, making sure you have a dedicated structure for your revision schedule."
前教师、一家私人辅导公司的创始人帕特里克・威尔逊（Patrick Wilson）说：“要真正感到自信并克服那种令人反胃的考试焦虑，最好的办法是提前为每场考试做好准备，确保你有一个专门的复习计划表。”

11
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:19,920
Wilson helped to create a guide for avoiding the last-minute jitters.
威尔逊协助编写了一份避免临考紧张的指南。

12
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:27,890
It advises the revision timetable to start up to ten weeks before the exam, dividing learning into chunks.
该指南建议复习时间表要在考试前十周就开始制定，将学习内容分成组块。

13
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:30,500
Don't overload yourself.
不要给自己过多负担。

14
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,550
Students should also give themselves regular rewards and breaks during revision.
学生们在复习期间也应该定期给自己一些奖励和休息时间。

15
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:39,970
People learn things in different ways and this should be taken into account.
人们学习的方式各不相同，这一点应该被考虑进去。

16
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:42,880
I learn better by reading things out loud.
通过大声朗读，我的学习效果会更好。

17
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:49,200
Some colleagues believe colour-coordinating notes according to subject can produce good results too.
一些同事认为，按照科目用适当的颜色记笔记也能取得不错的效果。

18
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:54,090
But there's a consensus against spending the night before the exam studying.
但大家有一个共识，就是反对在考试前一晚学习。

19
00:01:54,090 --> 00:01:59,510
If you don't get enough sleep, not even good luck underwear will help you pass the test.
如果你睡眠不足，即使是穿幸运内裤也无法帮你通过考试。
